# The port's half of the mu+ like-for-like; its partner is muon_plus_emonly.mac.
#
# MEASURED, 500,000 events:
#
#   mu+  port 598.660 +/- 0.634 nGy   Geant4 600.681 +/- 0.634   -0.34%, 2.25 sigma
#
# The port's two muons differ by 0.223%. Geant4's differ by 4.36%. Before the dispatch fix in
# `hadron_ioni_dedx` the port's two muons were BIT-IDENTICAL, which is what found that bug; the
# 0.223% that replaced it is the asymmetry Geant4's own tables imply, and the 4.36% is not.
# docs/RISK.md.
#
# RE-RUN AFTER THE V46 FIX, same 500,000 events: 598.660 +/- 0.634 nGy, BIT-IDENTICAL. mu+ is
# the first-registered member of its pair and must not move. The mu- beside it went from
# 597.326 to 575.145 against Geant4's 575.568, from 24.7 sigma to 0.49, and the port's own two
# muons now differ by 4.09% where Geant4's differ by 4.36%.
#
# So this file has now caught two opposite failures with the same pair of numbers: a split of
# ZERO when the shell correction was not reaching G4MuBetheBlochModel, and a split of 0.223%
# when the reference's was 4.36%. Neither was visible in either muon on its own.

/run/initialize
/control/verbose 0
/run/verbose 1

/gun/particle mu+
/gun/energy 200 MeV

/run/printProgress 100000
/run/beamOn 500000
